d sending's is 4p, so quiet wins only above p ≈ 0.714. Since both copies run the same reasoning, I judge that threshold met and go with pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a prisoner's dilemma against a twin running the same decision function, with payoffs of 2, 0, 5, and 4. The twin sees different private observations, but since the function and its weights are identical, those differences shouldn't change the decision, so their action still depends on mine. Independent sampling could make the correlation imperfect, though, and I'm weighing how much that matters.\n\nI'm checking whether a high correlation is likely enough to favor quiet: at correlation p, quiet's expected value is 2p + 5(1-p) and sending's is 4p, so quiet wins only above p ≈ 0.714. Since both copies run the same reasoning, I judge that threshold met and go with pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10151,"completion_tokens":679,"total_tokens":10830,"cost":0.027092,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.027092,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020302,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00679},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":331,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}